cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Powerlifting Strength Dynamics"
message: >-
  If you use this software, benchmark, or canonical schema in academic work,
  please cite it as software. This project is pre-alpha: no peer-reviewed
  paper describes the benchmark results yet, and PSD is not a validated
  physiological model.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PSD contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Litju/PowerliftingStrengthDynamics"
url: "https://github.com/Litju/PowerliftingStrengthDynamics"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Powerlifting Strength Dynamics (PSD) is an open benchmark for longitudinal
  system identification and rollout simulation of strength adaptation in
  powerlifting. It defines a canonical, event-time representation of complete
  powerlifting athlete histories that separates prescription, execution,
  observation, and outcome, preserves source provenance and missingness, and
  keeps real and synthetic data explicitly separable. PSD evaluates whether a
  model has identified useful multi-step dynamics, not isolated one-rep-max
  prediction, and imposes no physiological latent-state ontology.
keywords:
  - powerlifting
  - sports-science
  - system-identification
  - longitudinal-data
  - benchmark
  - time-series
  - partial-observation
  - parquet
  - reproducibility
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
